#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184031 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22d992a1-2ea8-5226-9971-188447f98ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Higher-Degree Taylor Polynomial Of a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "05dec044-4b3b-5f42-88c5-b7ab323b0e97" :question/math-academy-id "e-743" :question/problem "Let $f(x) = \\sin{x}$. Calculate the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$." :question/worked-solution "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nP_4(x) = f(a) + f'(a)(x-a) + \\dfrac{f''(a)}{2!}(x-a)^2 + \\dfrac{f'''(a)}{3!}(x-a)^3 + \\dfrac{f^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^4\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\na=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{4}(x) &= f(\\frac{π}{2}) + f^{′}(\\frac{π}{2})(x - \\frac{π}{2}) + (f^{″}(\\frac{π}{2}))/(2!)(x - \\frac{π}{2})^{2} \\\\\n&= + (f^{‴}(\\frac{π}{2}))/(3!)(x - \\frac{π}{2})^{3} + (f^{(4)}(\\frac{π}{2}))/(4!)(x - \\frac{π}{2})^{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need to work out\n\n$$\nf\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\n$$\nf'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\n$$\nf''\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\n$$\nf'''\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nf^{(4)}\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}f(x) &= \\sin x & ⟹ & f(\\frac{π}{2})|= 1 \\\\ f^{′}(x)|= \\cos x & ⟹ & f^{′}(\\frac{π}{2})|= 0 \\\\ f^{″}(x)|=-\\sin x & ⟹ & f^{″}(\\frac{π}{2})|=-1 \\\\ f^{‴}(x)|=-\\cos x & ⟹ & f^{‴}(\\frac{π}{2})|= 0 \\\\ f^{(4)}(x)|= \\sin x & ⟹ & f^{(4)}(\\frac{π}{2})|= 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P_4(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_{4}(x) &= 1 - \\frac{1}{2!}(x - \\frac{π}{2})^{2} + \\frac{1}{4!}(x - \\frac{π}{2})^{4} \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{1}{2}(x - \\frac{π}{2})^{2} + \\frac{1}{24}(x - \\frac{π}{2})^{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184032 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a832b1a2-e80e-53d0-bb64-03df0f1a209c" :knowledge-point/title "Obtaining a Higher-Order Derivative Of a Function Given its Higher-Degree Taylor Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "38bd1eff-19ac-5922-aa68-f9c30c9f5ea3" :question/math-academy-id "e-744" :question/problem "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=0$ is given by\n\n$P_4(x) = 1+2x-3x^2+4x^3-5x^4$.\n\nWhat is $f^{(4)}(0)$?" :question/worked-solution "The coefficient of $x^4$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{f^{(4)}(0)}{4!}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(f^{(4)}(0))/(4!) &= -5 \\\\\n(f^{(4)}(0))/(24) &= -5 \\\\\nf^{(4)}(0) &= -120\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "22d992a1-2ea8-5226-9971-188447f98ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Higher-Degree Taylor Polynomial Of a Given Function About a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b067f957-d1a2-5a4e-9cc1-77ef98ced350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1) - \\frac{1}{3}(x - 1)^{2} + \\frac{1}{9}(x - 1)^{3} - \\frac{1}{27}(x - 1)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183654} {:answer/id #uuid "e7962fc0-d6f6-55b5-bfbe-f3a68b0b2f66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1) - \\frac{1}{2}(x - 1)^{2} + \\frac{1}{8}(x - 1)^{3} - \\frac{1}{24}(x - 1)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183655} {:answer/id #uuid "0a76b62e-b61a-5426-ab29-5d735f853c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1) - \\frac{1}{2}(x - 1)^{2} + \\frac{1}{6}(x - 1)^{3} - \\frac{1}{24}(x - 1)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183656} {:answer/id #uuid "53bcda49-0258-5ddc-b1c0-266c6abcb7ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1) - \\frac{1}{2}(x - 1)^{2} + \\frac{1}{3}(x - 1)^{3} - \\frac{1}{4}(x - 1)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183657} {:answer/id #uuid "701bd027-8eac-5b27-a63e-b6984de17650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1) - \\frac{1}{2}(x - 1)^{2} + \\frac{1}{4}(x - 1)^{3} - \\frac{1}{8}(x - 1)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53bcda49-0258-5ddc-b1c0-266c6abcb7ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1) - \\frac{1}{2}(x - 1)^{2} + \\frac{1}{3}(x - 1)^{3} - \\frac{1}{4}(x - 1)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183657} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ffebf51-6796-5f35-bc21-9d52c4bedcbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183653}] :question/id #uuid "3b85ecd4-54ac-5495-9245-f4b1757d55a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-8174" :question/problem "Find the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $\\ln x$ about $x = 1$."}]}
